@startuml
!theme plain
title M1 leak-safe provider startup and mandatory-failure ordering
actor "Containing app" as App
participant "Packet-tunnel provider" as Provider
participant "Profile and Keychain boundary" as Profile
participant "SSH bootstrap" as SSH
participant "Packet plane and private TCP adapter" as Packet
participant "Tunnel DNS over SSH TCP" as DNS
participant "Network Extension settings" as NE
participant "Packet flow" as Flow

App -> Provider: Start with opaque profile reference
Provider -> Profile: Load non-secret snapshot and credential references
Profile --> Provider: Validated generation
Provider -> SSH: Resolve on physical path, connect, verify host, authenticate
SSH --> Provider: Verified session plus actual endpoint
Provider -> Packet: Prepare bridge, HEV, private SOCKS, TCP admission
Packet --> Provider: Ready without packet reads
Provider -> DNS: Prepare virtual UDP and TCP listener plus SSH DNS-over-TCP
DNS --> Provider: Safe DNS ready, no physical fallback
Provider -> NE: Apply IPv4 and IPv6 defaults, tunnel DNS, exact SSH host exclusion
NE --> Provider: Settings applied
Provider -> Flow: Start packet reads
Flow --> Provider: Read loop active
Provider --> App: Versioned TCP and safe-DNS capability snapshot

note over Provider,Flow
The provider owns all live state.
App suspension or termination does not stop forwarding.
end note

alt Mandatory failure before settings apply
  Provider -> DNS: Cancel if acquired
  Provider -> Packet: Cancel and release if acquired
  Provider -> SSH: Close session if acquired
  Provider --> App: Failed with no tunnel routes installed
else Mandatory failure after settings apply
  Provider -> Flow: Stop reads and new flows
  Provider -> DNS: Stop transactions without physical fallback
  Provider -> Packet: Cancel flows and release packet plane
  Provider -> SSH: Close session
  Provider -> NE: Remove or invalidate tunnel settings through provider stop
  Provider --> App: Capability revoked, then explicit failure
end
@enduml